"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f9c59a-257d-52f2-ab08-6986d283c94a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-314141"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-3772/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "f9095015-a714-58c6-a9c8-666c90d50069" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3772/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "07ed3234-46d2-5b36-9370-76bf480310fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3772/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "2ced3304-7ac4-50f7-b4da-3f2fd40f375b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3772/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "cb035e8f-016b-5e19-bf2b-3c46ffe24954" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3772/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "0a492da3-244e-53e9-8fc1-0a82171cc58c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-3772/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bb657fe6-a6b6-552c-89eb-f7d5167bedb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-3772/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-3772/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" "q-3772/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-3772/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-3772/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-3772/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-3772" :question/id #uuid "523acc35-7db0-52db-b989-53904d8cc74c" :question/math-academy-id "q-3772" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{4}-1}{x-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Note that plugging in $x=1$ gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ However, we can use L'Hopital's rule to find this limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{4}-1}{x-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{[{x}^{4}-1]^{′}}{[x-1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{1} \\\\  & =4(1)^{3} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-3772/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f9c59a-257d-52f2-ab08-6986d283c94a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-3772"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336939/field-1/327774e6fa81a03b193afe973642718732d81aa2fc829bee688b641b7603e9eb" :answer/id #uuid "506d9697-ea2a-524d-a154-f90f148c8016" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336939/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc93b39c-eb23-566a-930e-a415dee59caf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336939/field-1/327774e6fa81a03b193afe973642718732d81aa2fc829bee688b641b7603e9eb" :answer-field/choices ["q-336939/field-1/327774e6fa81a03b193afe973642718732d81aa2fc829bee688b641b7603e9eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336939" :question/id #uuid "f590b133-99f7-591b-b6c9-d85e4d4334e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-336939" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x}{{x}^{2}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=0$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x}{{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x]}^{′}}{[{x}^{2}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{5}{1+5x}-5)}{2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{1+5x}-1)}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+5x)-5x}{{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{1+5x}-1)}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[(1+5x)^{-1}-1]}^{′}}{[x]^{′}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{x\\to 0}(-5(1+5x)^{-2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(-5) \\\\  & =-\\frac{25}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336939/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a41d750-ffd9-5226-9bd7-b763575870c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336939"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336899/field-1/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328" :answer/id #uuid "e7f9b1ad-6574-5f0a-98e2-03b07773efc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336899/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "429278f0-2f1d-561f-b7b3-f0620da95645" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336899/field-1/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328" :answer-field/choices ["q-336899/field-1/29f1bd004b0e742e8153de2e3a77945bac059aed56c8ead2bc0011a45597d328"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336899" :question/id #uuid "7b1ee7cf-14c4-52ed-a4c9-8bd4dbb68e27" :question/math-academy-id "q-336899" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n$\\,{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we plug in $x=1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[{x}^{2}-2x+1]}^{′}}{{[({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{2x-2}{4x({x}^{2}-9)+32} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{2{x}^{3}-18x+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{x}^{2}-2x+1}{({x}^{2}-9)^{2}+32x-96} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{x-1}{2{x}^{3}-18x+16} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{[x-1]}^{′}}{{[2{x}^{3}-18x+16]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{1}{6{x}^{2}-18} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6(1)^{2}-18} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336899/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8a41d750-ffd9-5226-9bd7-b763575870c1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336899"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72338/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "e08c345f-a195-5ac3-9c75-8fb006a80092" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72338/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "fa54ee09-bffa-5369-a378-ab3cb86879fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72338/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "732f3e75-c4b6-5940-bff8-1f15ccab93dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72338/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "5b54ea7b-9a7f-56c4-92a9-a7b561334ccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72338/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "322bb0f8-d34c-5d73-beef-4d732d5c751f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72338/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "536f7004-0d40-5805-8c75-5fc73256ef67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72338/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-72338/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" "q-72338/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-72338/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-72338/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-72338/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72338" :question/id #uuid "053d9468-0f05-5921-951a-24e8dcf2b789" :question/math-academy-id "q-72338" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})}{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+8)}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+8)=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}})}{(\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+8)} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}]}^{′}}{{[\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}+8]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{(-\\frac{6}{{x}^{7}})}{(-\\frac{4}{{x}^{5}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{6{x}^{-7}}{4{x}^{-5}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{3}{2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-72338/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f29435f-b112-5999-b0ca-9003d9e622e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72338"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336777/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "975a2b7b-f0d4-596a-9ae7-9c1ffed9b7d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336777/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1f997f2c-5557-55bd-b731-4b16a4585873" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336777/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b4a3fe-cd2b-575e-938e-063e953635ff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336777/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-336777/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" "q-336777/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336777" :question/id #uuid "27356911-a306-56f7-a4fc-02e38fb05909" :question/math-academy-id "q-336777" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}+1)}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}(\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}+1)=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{(\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}+1)}{(\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}})} & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{[\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}}+1]}^{′}}{{[\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{(-\\frac{9}{{x}^{4}})}{(-\\frac{4}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{x}^{-4}}{{x}^{-3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336777/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f29435f-b112-5999-b0ca-9003d9e622e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336777"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336790/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3de1fde5-b622-518b-ad82-82149805110c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336790/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "18b2c6a1-89fb-570b-8112-700a06af6483" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336790/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-336790/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336790" :question/id #uuid "6fbc02c6-b501-5eec-8b59-c16ce48b0e6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-336790" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {(\\pi /2)}^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{sec}⁡x]}^{′}}{{[{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}{{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}\\frac{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}\\cancel{(\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (\\pi /2)^{-}}\\frac{1}{{e}^{\\operatorname{sec}⁡x}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336790/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f29435f-b112-5999-b0ca-9003d9e622e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336790"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336967/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "a8bd0a17-4706-5928-8600-0383bcf572b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336967/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4c0221-1b1c-59d0-9d62-8285e27c9a0c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336967/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer-field/choices ["q-336967/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336967" :question/id #uuid "f2d95c01-9555-57f8-b02b-000768fa79cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-336967" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}+\\sqrt{x}}{{x}^{2}-5\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}+\\sqrt{x}}{{x}^{2}-5\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[{x}^{2}+\\sqrt{x}]^{′}}{[{x}^{2}-5\\sqrt{x}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}}{2x-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{x}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{2}+\\sqrt{x}}{{x}^{2}-5\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{[2x+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}]}^{′}}{{[2x-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{x}}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{[2x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}]}^{′}}{{[2x-\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{-1/2}]}^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{-3/2}}{2+\\frac{5}{4}{x}^{-3/2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{2-\\frac{1}{4{x}^{3/2}}}{2+\\frac{5}{4{x}^{3/2}}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-336967/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336967"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-336956/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "3f695ca6-76e6-5a28-b810-7fc56c04ff32" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336956/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3c42912c-d1b4-5c7a-8839-77c7522e4cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336956/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b8aa0da-cf0d-5f4a-9baf-094168258a5a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-336956/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-336956/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" "q-336956/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336956" :question/id #uuid "38d3cf83-bd89-5be8-bd8f-dc1bce7bfe18" :question/math-academy-id "q-336956" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3x+\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have an indeterminate form of type $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty },$ so applying L'Hopital's rule yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{3x+\\sqrt{x}}{\\sqrt{x}} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[3x+\\sqrt{x}]^{′}}{[\\sqrt{x}]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(3+\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})}{\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(6\\sqrt{x}+1) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336956/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aeebf57f-21dc-558a-bec5-4e97a5b26de4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336956"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115519/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "7a58d85f-54b0-5066-8718-27b52202e334" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115519/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "76bbb6ff-a567-53d8-a9ef-bfda58cd60c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115519/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "a2d0917b-d5e5-5853-803a-4431540b20b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115519/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "c892f45c-edec-52aa-9d8e-808acbc0e409" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115519/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "2922593b-f08f-513a-a291-4e6e39a50861" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-